title ALES76 — Lotus's auto-pan, the same LFO swept across the stereo field
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first, take the next agent-doable lap, approve own design rounds, send each finished increment, stop at custody gates
think Both ALES74 (tremolo) and ALES75 (ring modulator) closed on the same named next rung — auto-pan, the same triangle LFO on the stereo field. It is the modulation family's third and last target: the LFO drove a DELAY (chorus/vibrato/flanger), then AMPLITUDE (tremolo/ring modulator), and now POSITION. Lindy-first the durable primitive is already there — ALES10's linear pan and its StereoClip; crux-first the recognition is one sentence: auto-pan IS ALES10's linear pan swept across time, exactly as ALES12 saw a crossfade to be an equal-power pan swept across an overlap. No new LFO, no new sum.
think The genuine new correctness, not a restatement of ALES10: ALES10 preserved left + right == mono by folding each channel's weight into its own fader — two independent @divTrunc divisions, which preserve the sum only where the split falls on a whole sample. Auto-pan STRENGTHENS the invariant to hold exactly at every sample for every signal by computing the far channel as the RESIDUAL of the near — right[i] = saturate(x·pos/glide_scale), left[i] = saturate(x − right[i]) — the same residual move ALES42's tone stack used for its mid band. So left + right == src byte-for-byte, never x − 1.
think Because the position stays a non-negative attenuation weight (0 ≤ pos ≤ glide_scale), each channel is a fraction of the dry, so both sit in the i16 rail and the write's saturate is a proven no-op — auto-pan is the tremolo's non-negative kin, NOT the ring modulator's bipolar one (no sign flip, no two's-complement corner). It reads the mono source and writes a fresh StereoClip: the source is READ-ONLY, a stereo render rather than an in-place edit, so it pans the whole clip rather than a span.
think Faults: BadPeriod (period not a positive multiple of four or past max_clip), BadDepth (negative depth or swing floor past hard-left below 0), BadPan (swing top past hard-right above glide_scale). No BadGain (the denominator is the fixed glide_scale, never a caller's divide), no BadDelay, no BadRange on a span (the whole clip renders and out shares the source bound — asserted, never a live error). Proved the sum invariant under a full swing including sample_min; a hand-computed sweep (128 → 256 → 128 → 0) matches; a depth-0 auto-pan is a static pan; the source is unchanged; both channels stay in the rail; each fault refuses by name with src and out untouched.
obs GREEN on the first build across all six laws — no RED. The residual construction made ALES10's sum invariant exact per sample, asserted in the loop (left + right == dry) and proven again in the witness including sample_min. tame_style_check bans clean, ratchets printed; the new file carries well above two asserts per fn. Self-approved design round (no custody gate — bounded in-process i16 PCM rendered to a StereoClip, no network/keys/funds/device/speaker/sample-rate). The modulation family's three LFO targets — delay, amplitude, position — are now all proven.
loom witness=ales_auto_pan_witness laws=6 green=1 reuses=triangle_delay_at,StereoClip,glide_scale glide_scale=256 far_channel=residual sum_invariant=exact_per_sample saturate=noop snapshot=none source=read_only
